<p>The only browser that people really care about which falls into that group is IE6, and it has a bug in which it treats <code>height</code> and <code>min-height</code> for <code>overflow: visible</code> content anyway. So:</p>

<pre><code>#foo { 
  height: 10em;
  min-height: 10em;
}

html&gt;body #foo {
  height: auto;
}
</code></pre>

